    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0504" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100K77/79.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Dominican Minister to the
                            Assistant Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the Dominican Republic</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I take very great pleasure in
                    transmitting to you the cablegram that I received yesterday from the Dominican
                    Government, relative to the journey of his excellency Mr. Knox; it expressly
                    confirms my anticipations, which I have already had the honor to express to you.
                    It reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Communicate to the Department of State that the Dominican Government will
                            receive with the greatest pleasure the visit of the illustrious
                            Secretary, Mr. Knox. Machado, Secretary.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fran’co J. Peynado.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
